# An imported HTML page sits on a Letter page with Outlook-like margins
# (#1928): 15 px (225 twips) on every side, not Word's 1" (96 px). A Web
# Page still opens in Web Layout, which keeps its own padding and never
# reads page margins; View > Print Layout draws the page with the
# section's margins. The ruler probe reads the text's inset from the
# page's left and top edges in px at 100%, one more than the margin (as
# `doc-rulers.uit` reads a 144 px margin as 145): 16 here, 97 with 1".
# The text column is the 786 px body less the same px on each side.

test issue 1928 an imported html page has outlook like margins
  open copy:../fixtures/rounded-images.html
  call doc {}
  assert reply.view.layout is web
  call ribbon-click {"tab":"View","command":"ruler"}
  call ribbon-click {"tab":"View","command":"Print Layout"}
  shot window
  call doc {}
  assert reply.view.layout is print
  assert reply.view.zoom is 1
  assert reply.ruler.text_inset is 16
  assert reply.ruler.vtop_inset is 16
  assert reply.flow.text_column.width is 784
